2026-06-26 01:12:56,370 | AGENT | TechnicalArchitect Agent answered: Our company's platform, Atelier, is a Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) platform that provides a median latency of 1.3 seconds for common queries, with a p95 latency below 2 seconds. This meets the client's requirement for response times. 

Atelier also has standard connectors and custom adapters for SIH/DPI integration, which can facilitate seamless integration with existing hospital information systems and electronic patient records.

In terms of health interoperability standards, our platform supports HL7/FHIR through its health interoperability framework alignment with Ségur/Mon espace santé–DMP, and we have a delivery partner, Ligeo Santé, that helps with this integration.

For data sovereignty, our hosting options include the Sovereign HDS tier on OuraneCloud, which is SecNumCloud-qualified, HDS-certified, and EU-only. This ensures that data is hosted exclusively within the European Union and meets the client's requirements for data sovereignty.

We can propose an architecture where Atelier is deployed on the Sovereign HDS tier of OuraneCloud, with standard connectors and custom adapters for SIH/DPI integration. Our API-first approach (REST + webhook) with documented APIs will enable easy embedding in existing work environments. Additionally, our support for SAML, OIDC, LDAP, and Entra ID user directories ensures secure identity management.

